==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|school mate}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|school|-mate|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|sko͞ol′māt′}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈskuːlˌmeɪt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈskulˌmeɪt/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-schoolmate.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who was a fellow [[attendee]] at one's [[school]].
#: {{ux|en|I've lost touch with all my old '''schoolmates''': I only see them at class reunions.}}
#* {{RQ:Hawthorne Scarlet Letter|Introduction|text=The truth seems to be, however, that when he casts his leaves forth upon the wind, the author addresses, not the many who will fling aside his volume, or never take it up, but the few who will understand him better than most of his '''schoolmates''' or lifemates.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[schoolfriend]]; a [[friend]] from one's [[school]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|fellow}} {{q|obsolete slang}}; {{l|en|schoolfellow}}

====Hyponyms====
